#!/usr/bin/env python

"""a subtitle converter that generates ASS.

   this was bornt because Aegisub's "karaoke templater"
    (yes, it can be used for things other than lyrics if you set karaoke timing to zero)
    doesn't work with line breaks and doesn't stack subtitles.

   we want this for ordinary furigana / ruby texts to work in Mpv.
   so this program has a mini layout engine which should implement the features we need.

   it has a dependency on Qt because it's much more easy to just use shaping engine from it.
    (Aegisub uses wxWidgets similarly to measure texts for its "karaoke templater".)"""

